<title>USA: U.S. Feb business inventories rose 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb business inventories rose 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. February business inventories rose 0.3 percent after rising a revised 0.4 percent in January. It said February business sales rose 1.4 percent after rising 1.2 percent in January.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: February   January----(Prev)  December</p>
<p>Total Business  1,016.80  1,013.63  1,011.11  1,009.74  Durable Goods     611.87    609.31    607.69    606.89</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  404.93    404.32    403.42    402.85</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: February   January---(Prev)   December</p>
<p> Manufacturers     441.76   440.02    438.15   437.92</p>
<p> Retailers	   314.99   313.50    312.16   313.71</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     88.17    87.73     87.48</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 260.05   260.10    260.80   258.11</p>
<p>    SALES:	 February   January---(Prev)   December</p>
<p> Total Business    746.27   735.85    735.93   727.43</p>
<p> Durable Goods     369.63   361.33    361.70   357.90</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  376.64   374.52    374.23   369.53</p>
<p>    SALES:	 February   January---(Prev)   December</p>
<p> Manufacturers     321.46   318.50    318.69   315.28</p>
<p> Retailers	   215.14   211.96    211.46   208.32</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     53.89    52.17     52.10</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 209.67   205.40    205.79   203.84</p>
<p> Inventory-To-   February   January---(Prev)   December</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.36     1.38	1.37     1.39</p>
<p>The department said that the 1.4 percent increase in sales during February was the strongest for any month since April 1996, when they also rose 1.4 percent.</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>The February inventory-to-sales ratio of 1.36 is the lowest since January 1982, when the department began tracking the ratio.</p>
<p>The department revised January business inventories from up 0.1 percent.</p>
